IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bgg3-nouns`
IMPORT `bgg3-seat`

-- bgg3-cases-seat: worked cases for the seat layer (bgg3-seat), one or more per question.
-- Each case is a person with facts they could state; the expected answer was decided by reading the
-- German text and written beside the case before the run.  JUST TRUE = the text says yes, JUST FALSE =
-- the text says no in its own words, NOTHING = the text does not decide (NOTES.md, section Reading a result).
-- Inputs follow the order of each question's GIVEN in bgg3-seat.l4.

§ `Civil matters (Art 72 to 77)`

-- Art 72 inputs: (civil matter, debt enforcement or bankruptcy, public-law decision, immediate connection with civil law, kind of public-law decision, pension foundation)
-- A tenant challenges an eviction judgment: a civil matter ("Entscheide in Zivilsachen").
#ASSERT `Art 72 the appeal in civil matters lies against my decision` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another kind of decision` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A creditor challenges a decision in bankruptcy proceedings (Art 72(2)(a)).
#ASSERT `Art 72 the appeal in civil matters lies against my decision` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `another kind of decision` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An owner challenges a land register authority's decision: public law, in immediate connection with civil law, and a listed kind (Art 72(2)(b)(2)).
#ASSERT `Art 72 the appeal in civil matters lies against my decision` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `keeping of a land, civil status, commercial or intellectual-property register` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A person challenges a public-law decision that has no immediate connection with civil law and is not a listed kind: the text does not decide.
#ASSERT `Art 72 the appeal in civil matters lies against my decision` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `another kind of decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A pension institution challenges the supervisory decision about it: item (4) leaves out pension and vested-benefits institutions ("mit Ausnahme der Vorsorge- und Freizügigkeitseinrichtungen"), and the person states no immediate connection: not covered.
#ASSERT `Art 72 the appeal in civil matters lies against my decision` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `supervision of foundations` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A case outside the encoding: not a civil, debt, or public-law decision at all.
#ASSERT `Art 72 the appeal in civil matters lies against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another kind of decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 73 input: (decision made in trade-mark opposition proceedings).  POLARITY SWAP: JUST TRUE = the Act excludes my decision from the appeal.
-- A trade-mark owner challenges a decision made in opposition proceedings: "Die Beschwerde ist unzulässig gegen Entscheide, die im Rahmen des Widerspruchsverfahrens gegen eine Marke getroffen worden sind": excluded.
-- EXPECTED VALUE CHANGED 2026-11-18: was JUST FALSE on the question `Art 73 the appeal in civil matters is admissible against my decision`.
#ASSERT `Art 73 my decision is excluded from the appeal in civil matters` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A party to any other civil decision: Art 73 does not decide the case.  (Unchanged: NOTHING.)
#ASSERT `Art 73 my decision is excluded from the appeal in civil matters` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 74(1) inputs: (pecuniary matter, employment law case, tenancy law case, value in francs)
-- An employee sues for 15000 francs: "mindestens beträgt: ... a. 15 000 Franken in arbeits- und mietrechtlichen Fällen".
#ASSERT `Art 74(1) the value in dispute in my case is enough` TRUE TRUE FALSE 15000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same employee with 14999 francs: the appeal is "nur zulässig" from 15000.
#ASSERT `Art 74(1) the value in dispute in my case is enough` TRUE TRUE FALSE 14999 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A tenant at 15000 francs.
#ASSERT `Art 74(1) the value in dispute in my case is enough` TRUE FALSE TRUE 15000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A buyer of goods (neither employment nor tenancy) at 30000 and at 29999 francs.
#ASSERT `Art 74(1) the value in dispute in my case is enough` TRUE FALSE FALSE 30000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 74(1) the value in dispute in my case is enough` TRUE FALSE FALSE 29999 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A matter that is not pecuniary: the limit is for "In vermögensrechtlichen Angelegenheiten" only, so the text does not decide.
#ASSERT `Art 74(1) the value in dispute in my case is enough` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 74(2) inputs: (pecuniary, employment, tenancy, value, legal question of fundamental importance, federal statute provides a single cantonal instance, cantonal supervisory authority in debt/bankruptcy, bankruptcy and composition judge, deciding body)
-- A buyer at 20000 francs (short of 30000) whose case raises a legal question of fundamental importance (Art 74(2)(a)).
#ASSERT `Art 74(2) the appeal is admissible in my case although the value is short` TRUE FALSE FALSE 20000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `last cantonal instance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A buyer at 20000 francs with no ground at all: the subsection gives no saving on these facts.
#ASSERT `Art 74(2) the appeal is admissible in my case although the value is short` TRUE FALSE FALSE 20000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `last cantonal instance` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A debtor at 100 francs against a decision of the bankruptcy and composition judge (Art 74(2)(d)).
#ASSERT `Art 74(2) the appeal is admissible in my case although the value is short` TRUE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `last cantonal instance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A patent holder at 100 francs against a decision of the Federal Patent Court (Art 74(2)(e)).
#ASSERT `Art 74(2) the appeal is admissible in my case although the value is short` TRUE FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `Federal Patent Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The value reaches the limit (40000 francs): the subsection is not engaged.
#ASSERT `Art 74(2) the appeal is admissible in my case although the value is short` TRUE FALSE FALSE 40000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `last cantonal instance` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 75(1) input: (deciding body)
#ASSERT `Art 75(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `last cantonal instance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 75(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `Federal Administrative Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 75(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `Federal Patent Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A decision of some other body: the list is not closed with "nur", so the text does not decide.
#ASSERT `Art 75(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `another body` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 75(2) inputs: (last instance is an upper court, decided as appeal instance, federal statute gives a single instance, commercial court as single instance, action filed directly with consent, value in francs)
-- A litigant whose last cantonal instance was an upper court sitting on appeal.
#ASSERT `Art 75(2) my last cantonal instance is an upper court deciding as an appeal instance, or an exception applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A litigant whose case was decided by a commercial court as the single cantonal instance (exception (b)).
#ASSERT `Art 75(2) my last cantonal instance is an upper court deciding as an appeal instance, or an exception applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An action of 100000 francs filed directly with the upper court with all parties' consent (exception (c)).
#ASSERT `Art 75(2) my last cantonal instance is an upper court deciding as an appeal instance, or an exception applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same at 99999 francs: the exception does not apply, and nothing else holds: the text states no consequence for the person.
#ASSERT `Art 75(2) my last cantonal instance is an upper court deciding as an appeal instance, or an exception applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 99999 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 76(1) inputs: (took part before the lower instance, had no chance to take part, especially affected, interest worthy of protection)
-- The losing party who took part, is especially affected and has an interest.
#ASSERT `Art 76(1) I am entitled to appeal in civil matters` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A person who was not heard and had no chance to take part, and is affected.
#ASSERT `Art 76(1) I am entitled to appeal in civil matters` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A person who did not take part although they could have: item (a) fails.
#ASSERT `Art 76(1) I am entitled to appeal in civil matters` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A person who took part but is not especially affected: item (b) fails.
#ASSERT `Art 76(1) I am entitled to appeal in civil matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Art 77(1) inputs: (decision of an arbitral tribunal, international arbitration, national arbitration, conditions of PILA Arts 190-192 met, conditions of ZPO Arts 389-395 met)
-- A party to an international arbitration whose award meets the conditions of the Private International Law Act.
#ASSERT `Art 77(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against my arbitral award whatever the value in dispute` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A party to a national arbitration whose award meets the conditions of the Civil Procedure Code.
#ASSERT `Art 77(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against my arbitral award whatever the value in dispute` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A party to an international arbitration whose award does not meet those conditions: the grant is limited by its own wording ("unter den Voraussetzungen"): not covered.
#ASSERT `Art 77(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against my arbitral award whatever the value in dispute` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A decision that is not an arbitral award at all.
#ASSERT `Art 77(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against my arbitral award whatever the value in dispute` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 77(2) inputs: (appeal under Art 77(1), article number, paragraph number, the provision is used to let the Court decide itself)
-- Art 95 lies within "90–98": not applicable in these cases.
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the listed provision is applicable to my appeal against the arbitral award` TRUE 95 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Art 48 paragraph 3 is listed by name.
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the listed provision is applicable to my appeal against the arbitral award` TRUE 48 3 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Art 107 paragraph 2 is excluded only so far as it lets the Court decide the matter itself.
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the listed provision is applicable to my appeal against the arbitral award` TRUE 107 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the listed provision is applicable to my appeal against the arbitral award` TRUE 107 2 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 100 is not in the list: the text does not say whether it applies.
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the listed provision is applicable to my appeal against the arbitral award` TRUE 100 0 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The appeal is not under Art 77(1): outside this subsection.
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the listed provision is applicable to my appeal against the arbitral award` FALSE 95 0 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 77(2bis) input: (appeal under Art 77(1))
#ASSERT `Art 77(2bis) I may draft my written submission in English` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 77(2bis) I may draft my written submission in English` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 77(3) inputs: (appeal under Art 77(1), complaint raised in the appeal, complaint reasoned in the appeal)
-- "prüft nur Rügen, die in der Beschwerde vorgebracht und begründet worden sind".
#ASSERT `Art 77(3) my complaint meets the condition for being examined` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 77(3) my complaint meets the condition for being examined` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 77(3) my complaint meets the condition for being examined` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 77(3) my complaint meets the condition for being examined` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Criminal matters (Art 78 to 81)`

-- Art 78 inputs: (criminal matter, decision on civil claims, civil claims dealt with together with the criminal matter, decision on execution of penalties and measures)
-- A convicted person challenges the judgment: a criminal matter.
#ASSERT `Art 78 the appeal in criminal matters lies against my decision` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A victim challenges the decision on their civil claims, dealt with together with the criminal case (Art 78(2)(a)).
#ASSERT `Art 78 the appeal in criminal matters lies against my decision` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same, but the civil claims are not dealt with together: the item says "wenn" (a marginal reading, NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `Art 78 the appeal in criminal matters lies against my decision` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A prisoner challenges a decision on the execution of a sentence (Art 78(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `Art 78 the appeal in criminal matters lies against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A case outside the encoding: none of the four.
#ASSERT `Art 78 the appeal in criminal matters lies against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 79 inputs: (deciding body, decision on coercive measures).  POLARITY SWAP: JUST TRUE = the Act excludes my decision from the appeal.
-- The Complaints Chamber of the Federal Criminal Court decided something that is not a coercive measure: excluded ("unzulässig gegen Entscheide der Beschwerdekammer des Bundesstrafgerichts, soweit es sich nicht um Entscheide über Zwangsmassnahmen handelt").
-- EXPECTED VALUE CHANGED 2026-11-18: was JUST FALSE on the question `Art 79 the appeal in criminal matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance`.
#ASSERT `Art 79 my decision of the Complaints Chamber is excluded from the appeal in criminal matters` `Federal Criminal Court Complaints Chamber` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same chamber on a coercive measure: "soweit es sich nicht um Entscheide über Zwangsmassnahmen handelt": the bar does not reach it, and Art 79 does not say the appeal is admissible: not covered.  (Unchanged: NOTHING.)
#ASSERT `Art 79 my decision of the Complaints Chamber is excluded from the appeal in criminal matters` `Federal Criminal Court Complaints Chamber` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A decision of the Appeals Chamber: the bar names only the Complaints Chamber.  (Unchanged: NOTHING.)
#ASSERT `Art 79 my decision of the Complaints Chamber is excluded from the appeal in criminal matters` `Federal Criminal Court Appeals Chamber` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A decision of a last cantonal instance, not on a coercive measure: outside the bar.  (New case, 2026-11-18: NOTHING.)
#ASSERT `Art 79 my decision of the Complaints Chamber is excluded from the appeal in criminal matters` `last cantonal instance` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 80(1) input: (deciding body)
#ASSERT `Art 80(1) the appeal in criminal matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `last cantonal instance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 80(1) the appeal in criminal matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `Federal Criminal Court Appeals Chamber` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 80(1) the appeal in criminal matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `Federal Criminal Court Complaints Chamber` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A decision of another body: the list is not closed with "nur".
#ASSERT `Art 80(1) the appeal in criminal matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `another body` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 80(2) inputs: (last instance is an upper court, decided as appeal instance, the Code of Criminal Procedure has an upper court or coercive-measures court decide as single instance)
#ASSERT `Art 80(2) my last cantonal instance is an upper court deciding as an appeal instance, or the exception applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The exception: a coercive-measures court decided as the single cantonal instance.
#ASSERT `Art 80(2) my last cantonal instance is an upper court deciding as an appeal instance, or the exception applies` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 80(2) my last cantonal instance is an upper court deciding as an appeal instance, or the exception applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 81(1) inputs: (took part, no chance to take part, role, decision on detention, decision can affect civil claims, appeal concerns the right to file the complaint as such, other legally protected interest)
-- The accused, who took part.
#ASSERT `Art 81(1) I am entitled to appeal in criminal matters` TRUE FALSE `accused person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The accused's legal representative, who took part.
#ASSERT `Art 81(1) I am entitled to appeal in criminal matters` TRUE FALSE `legal representative of the accused person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A private claimant whose civil claims the decision can affect (item 5).
#ASSERT `Art 81(1) I am entitled to appeal in criminal matters` TRUE FALSE `private claimant` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A private claimant whose civil claims cannot be affected and who states no other interest.
#ASSERT `Art 81(1) I am entitled to appeal in criminal matters` TRUE FALSE `private claimant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The public prosecutor's office on a decision about detention: item (3) says "ausser bei Entscheiden über die Anordnung, die Verlängerung und die Aufhebung der Untersuchungs- und Sicherheitshaft", and no other interest is stated.
#ASSERT `Art 81(1) I am entitled to appeal in criminal matters` TRUE FALSE `public prosecutor's office` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The public prosecutor's office on another decision (item 3).
#ASSERT `Art 81(1) I am entitled to appeal in criminal matters` TRUE FALSE `public prosecutor's office` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A person who filed the criminal complaint, appealing about the right to file it as such (item 6).
#ASSERT `Art 81(1) I am entitled to appeal in criminal matters` TRUE FALSE `person who files the criminal complaint` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An accused who did not take part before the lower instance although they could have: item (a) fails.
#ASSERT `Art 81(1) I am entitled to appeal in criminal matters` FALSE FALSE `accused person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An accused who had no chance to take part.
#ASSERT `Art 81(1) I am entitled to appeal in criminal matters` FALSE TRUE `accused person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Another person with a legally protected interest the "insbesondere" list does not name.
#ASSERT `Art 81(1) I am entitled to appeal in criminal matters` TRUE FALSE `another person` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Public-law matters (Art 82 to 89)`

-- Art 82 inputs: (public-law decision, cantonal enactment, political voting rights, popular election, popular vote)
#ASSERT `Art 82 the appeal in public-law matters lies against my decision` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A resident challenges a cantonal statute as such (Art 82(b)).
#ASSERT `Art 82 the appeal in public-law matters lies against my decision` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A voter challenges the result of a popular vote (Art 82(c)).
#ASSERT `Art 82 the appeal in public-law matters lies against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A case outside the encoding.
#ASSERT `Art 82 the appeal in public-law matters lies against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Art 83: which decisions are excluded`

-- A foreign national's ordinary naturalisation was refused: the list excludes such decisions (Art 83(b): "Die Beschwerde ist unzulässig gegen: ... b. Entscheide über die ordentliche Einbürgerung").
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(b) ordinary naturalisation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- A foreign national was refused a residence permit and no federal or international law gives a claim to it: excluded (Art 83(c)(2)).
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(c)(2) foreigners law: a permit` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- The same, but federal law gives a claim to the permit: the limb does not reach the case ("auf die weder das Bundesrecht noch das Völkerrecht einen Anspruch einräumt"): not covered.
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(c)(2) foreigners law: a permit` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- An asylum seeker's case was decided by the Federal Administrative Court and no extradition request is pending: excluded (Art 83(d)(1)).
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(d)(1) asylum: decision of the Federal Administrative Court` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- The same, but the state they flee has requested their extradition ("ausser sie betreffen Personen, gegen die ein Auslieferungsersuchen ... vorliegt"): not covered.
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(d)(1) asylum: decision of the Federal Administrative Court` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- A bidder lost a public tender: no legal question of fundamental importance arises and the contract is above the threshold: excluded by item (f)(1).
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(f) public procurement` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 600 500 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- A bidder lost a public tender: a legal question of fundamental importance arises and the estimated value (600) reaches the threshold (500): neither item (f)(1) nor (f)(2) bars the case: not covered.
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(f) public procurement` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 600 500 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The same, but the estimated value (400) is below the threshold (500): excluded by item (f)(2) although a legal question arises.
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(f) public procurement` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 400 500 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- A civil servant disputes a transfer, a matter that is not about money and not about equality of the sexes: excluded (Art 83(g)).
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(g) public-law employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- The same, but the matter concerns equality of the sexes ("nicht aber die Gleichstellung der Geschlechter betreffen"): not covered.
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(g) public-law employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- A taxpayer challenges administrative assistance given to a foreign authority in tax matters: the list excepts tax assistance ("mit Ausnahme der Amtshilfe in Steuersachen"), so item (h) does not reach it: not covered (Art 84a governs).
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(h) international administrative assistance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- A person challenges administrative assistance that is not in tax matters: excluded (Art 83(h)).
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(h) international administrative assistance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- A taxpayer's request for remission of a levy (not one of the listed taxes) was refused: excluded (Art 83(m)).
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(m) deferral or remission of levies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- A taxpayer's request for remission of the direct federal tax was refused and a legal question of fundamental importance arises: the departure lets the appeal in: the text says the decision is not excluded.
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(m) deferral or remission of levies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- A student challenges the result of an examination: excluded (Art 83(t)).
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(t) results of examinations and other ability assessments` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- A decision in the field of foreign affairs and international law gives a claim to judicial review: not covered ("soweit das Völkerrecht nicht einen Anspruch auf gerichtliche Beurteilung einräumt").
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(a) security, neutrality, diplomatic protection or other foreign affairs` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- A water-right concession for a plant, with a legal question of fundamental importance: not covered.
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `(zbis) water-right concessions for plants under Art 9a(3) of the Electricity Supply Act` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- A decision of none of the kinds in the list: the list does not say the appeal is admissible or not: not covered (outside the encoding).
#ASSERT `Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` `none of these kinds` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Arts 84 to 89`

-- Art 84 inputs: (legal assistance in criminal matters, subject, elementary procedural principles violated, serious defects abroad, particularly important for other reasons)
-- An extradition decision in a particularly important case (Art 84(1)).
#ASSERT `Art 84(1) the condition for an appeal on international legal assistance in criminal matters is met in my case` TRUE `extradition` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A seizure where there are grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated (Art 84(2): a particularly important case).
#ASSERT `Art 84(1) the condition for an appeal on international legal assistance in criminal matters is met in my case` TRUE `seizure` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An extradition decision, not a particularly important case: the appeal is "nur zulässig" in one.
#ASSERT `Art 84(1) the condition for an appeal on international legal assistance in criminal matters is met in my case` TRUE `extradition` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A decision on another subject in a particularly important case: the four subjects are the only ones.
#ASSERT `Art 84(1) the condition for an appeal on international legal assistance in criminal matters is met in my case` TRUE `another subject` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a legal assistance decision.
#ASSERT `Art 84(1) the condition for an appeal on international legal assistance in criminal matters is met in my case` FALSE `extradition` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 84a inputs: (tax administrative assistance, legal question of fundamental importance, elementary principles violated, serious defects abroad, particularly important for other reasons)
#ASSERT `Art 84a the condition for an appeal on international administrative assistance in tax matters is met in my case` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Particularly important within the meaning of Art 84(2): serious defects abroad.
#ASSERT `Art 84a the condition for an appeal on international administrative assistance in tax matters is met in my case` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 84a the condition for an appeal on international administrative assistance in tax matters is met in my case` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 84a the condition for an appeal on international administrative assistance in tax matters is met in my case` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 85(1) inputs: (pecuniary matter, state liability, public-law employment, value in francs)
-- A claimant for state liability at 29999 and at 30000 francs.
#ASSERT `Art 85(1) the appeal is admissible in my pecuniary matter` TRUE TRUE FALSE 29999 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 85(1) the appeal is admissible in my pecuniary matter` TRUE TRUE FALSE 30000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A public employee at 14999 and at 15000 francs.
#ASSERT `Art 85(1) the appeal is admissible in my pecuniary matter` TRUE FALSE TRUE 14999 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 85(1) the appeal is admissible in my pecuniary matter` TRUE FALSE TRUE 15000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A matter that is not pecuniary.
#ASSERT `Art 85(1) the appeal is admissible in my pecuniary matter` FALSE TRUE FALSE 100 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 85(2) inputs: (pecuniary matter, state liability, public-law employment, value in francs, legal question of fundamental importance)
#ASSERT `Art 85(2) the appeal is admissible in my case although the value is short` TRUE TRUE FALSE 29999 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 85(2) the appeal is admissible in my case although the value is short` TRUE TRUE FALSE 29999 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The value reaches the limit: not engaged.
#ASSERT `Art 85(2) the appeal is admissible in my case although the value is short` TRUE TRUE FALSE 30000 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 86(1) inputs: (deciding body, an appeal to the Federal Administrative Court is admissible)
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `Federal Administrative Court` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `Federal Criminal Court Appeals Chamber` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `independent complaints authority for radio and television` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A last cantonal instance, with no appeal to the Federal Administrative Court available.
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `last cantonal instance` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A last cantonal instance, but an appeal to the Federal Administrative Court is admissible ("sofern nicht").
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `last cantonal instance` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A decision of the Federal Patent Court: not one of the four bodies named.
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` `Federal Patent Court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 86(2) inputs: (the immediate lower instance is an upper court, another federal statute provides appeal from another judicial authority)
#ASSERT `Art 86(2) my immediate lower instance is an upper court, or another federal statute provides for appeal from another judicial authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(2) my immediate lower instance is an upper court, or another federal statute provides for appeal from another judicial authority` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(2) my immediate lower instance is an upper court, or another federal statute provides for appeal from another judicial authority` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 86(3) input: (decision of predominantly political character)
#ASSERT `Art 86(3) my canton may have set up an authority other than a court as immediate lower instance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(3) my canton may have set up an authority other than a court as immediate lower instance` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 87(1) inputs: (cantonal enactment, a cantonal remedy can be taken)
-- A resident challenges a cantonal ordinance and the canton gives no remedy: "unmittelbar die Beschwerde zulässig, sofern kein kantonales Rechtsmittel ergriffen werden kann".
#ASSERT `Art 87(1) the appeal lies directly against the cantonal enactment I challenge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 87(1) the appeal lies directly against the cantonal enactment I challenge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 87(1) the appeal lies directly against the cantonal enactment I challenge` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 87(2) inputs: (cantonal enactment, cantonal law provides a remedy against enactments)
#ASSERT `Art 87(2) Art 86 applies to my appeal against the cantonal enactment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 87(2) Art 86 applies to my appeal against the cantonal enactment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 88(1) inputs: (voting rights, election or vote; cantonal matter; act of the last cantonal instance; federal matter; ruling of the Federal Chancellery; decision of a cantonal government)
-- A voter challenges an act of the highest cantonal instance in a cantonal vote (item a).
#ASSERT `Art 88(1) the appeal on voting rights is admissible against the act I challenge` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A voter challenges a decision of a cantonal government in a federal vote (item b).
#ASSERT `Art 88(1) the appeal on voting rights is admissible against the act I challenge` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A voter challenges an act that is not of the last cantonal instance in a cantonal matter: the text does not decide.
#ASSERT `Art 88(1) the appeal on voting rights is admissible against the act I challenge` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 88(2) inputs: (the act can violate political rights in a cantonal matter, the act is an act of the parliament or the government)
#ASSERT `Art 88(2) my canton must provide a remedy against the act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Diese Pflicht erstreckt sich nicht auf Akte des Parlaments und der Regierung."
#ASSERT `Art 88(2) my canton must provide a remedy against the act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 88(2) my canton must provide a remedy against the act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Art 89(1) inputs: (took part before the lower instance, had no chance to take part, especially affected, interest worthy of protection)
#ASSERT `Art 89(1) I am entitled to appeal in public-law matters` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(1) I am entitled to appeal in public-law matters` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(1) I am entitled to appeal in public-law matters` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 89(1) I am entitled to appeal in public-law matters` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

